<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quingēnārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		quingeni. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Consisting of five hundred each</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cohortes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					5, 2, 3</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Consisting of five hundred</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thorax,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of five hundred pounds weight</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 20, 19, § 83</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanx,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					33, 11, 52, § 145</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poena,</span>”
				<i>a fine of five hundred asses</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 4, 14 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
